				{
					"type": "Text",
					"properties": {
						"text": "12. Sometimes neither bounds provider gives you the exact bounds you need. Enable the Position bounds checkbox. This allows you to manually adjust the bounds while keeping the skeleton fixed in place.\n\n13. With Position bounds enabled, drag the bounds handles to resize and reposition the collision area. Notice that Spineboy does not move - only the bounds change. Try making the bounds smaller, covering only Spineboy's feet.\n\n14. Click the Preview layout button. The red rectangle shows the custom bounds you defined. Spineboy collides with the platform using this smaller area. If you jump (up arrow), the head goes out now. Close the preview.\n\n15. Click the Reset bounds button. The bounds return to the calculated size based on the current Bounds provider setting.\n\n16. Congratulations! You completed the second tutorial. You learned how bounds determine the collision body used by behaviors, and how to customize them using different bounds providers and manual positioning. Go to the next one.",
